course: dictionary
lesson: 199
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning you need. Alarm is a good example. In «Smoke alarms give families time to escape», an alarm is a device, but in «set the alarm for six», it is a sound that wakes you up.
explain: «She cried out in alarm» uses alarm as a feeling: a sudden fear or worry. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Alarm can also be a verb, a doing word. «The sudden bang alarmed the birds» means the bang made the birds worried and frightened. The verb changes its ending to show time: alarm, alarms, alarmed, alarming.
fact: Alarm can be a noun (a thing or a feeling) or a verb (a doing word).
fact: «Alarm» can mean a device that makes a loud noise to warn people of danger, such as a smoke alarm.
fact: «Alarm» can mean a clock or phone sound that wakes you up at a set time.
fact: «Alarm» can mean a sudden feeling of fear or worry, as in «in alarm».
fact: As a verb, «alarm» means to make someone worried or frightened. A «false alarm» is a warning that turns out to be nothing.
exercise: «Smoke alarms give families time to escape.» What is an alarm in this sentence? | A clock that wakes you up | *A device that makes a loud noise to warn of danger | A feeling of fear inside your chest
exercise: «She cried out in alarm.» What does alarm mean here? | *A sudden feeling of fear or worry | A loud machine in a shop | A set time to get up
exercise: «The sudden bang alarmed the birds.» What does alarmed mean? | Woke the birds at a set time | Fed the birds | *Made the birds worried and frightened | Painted the birds bright colours
test: «Please set the alarm for seven o'clock.» What does alarm mean here? | *A sound that wakes you up at a set time | A smoke detector on the wall | To frighten someone | A feeling of fear
test: What is a «false alarm»? | *A warning that turns out to be nothing | A fire that is put out quickly | A bell that rings at school | A test that always passes
exam: Which sentence uses alarm as a verb (a doing word)? | «He set the alarm for six.» | *«The sudden flash of lightning alarmed the horse.» | «She cried out in alarm.» | «The smoke alarm beeped all night.»
